<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46174" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεῦγμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεύγνυμι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is used for joining,
				band, bond</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ζ. τοῦ
			λιμένος</span> the <i>barrier</i> of ships moored across the
			mouth of the harbour, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.69
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				13.14
			</span></i>:—written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεογμα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rev.Phil.</u>
				50.70
			</span></i> (Didyma, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bridge of boats,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.147
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antag.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ζ. τῶν ποταμῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					9.31
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.174e
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>pier</i> or <i>platform formed by lashing
				several vessels together</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.46.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>canal-lock,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PPetr.
				2p.123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3p.210
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεύγματ᾽
				ἀνάγκης</span>
			<i>the bonds</i> of necessity, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				443
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>zeugma</i>, a figure of speech, wherein two subjects are
			used jointly with the same predicate, which strictly belongs only to
			one, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				<u>Fig.</u>
				2.17
			</span></i>.</div>
